/guidance/using-ki/recommended-tools /docs/optional-tools/ 301

# What guidance had left was not a collection (KI-WEB-SITE-028). Once the project
# guides moved out, the directory held thirteen prompting guides for other vendors'
# models, their index, and one page about a reader's own machine — two unrelated
# things under a name that described neither, offered as a top-level section. Each
# half now lives at an address that says what it is. The splat covers the model
# pages without naming thirteen of them; the bare path needs its own rule because
# Cloudflare's splat does not match it.
/guidance/recommended-tools /docs/optional-tools/ 301
/guidance/prompting/* /docs/prompting/:splat 301
/guidance/prompting /docs/prompting/ 301
/guidance /docs/prompting/ 301

# Guidance became Docs (KI-WEB-SITE-037). A guide is one page of a finite body of
# material a reader works through, not a footnote to the repository it describes, so the
# pages left the projects they were filed under and the three standalone sections joined
# them: every address below was published and every one now resolves into /docs/.
#
# The project pages stay where they are — /projects/ is still the catalogue of what exists —
